<p>In the latest round of fighting, Israel carried out fresh strikes in Tehran while Iran launched missiles across Israel and elsewhere in the Middle East, extending a war that PBS said had entered its second month. President Trump said Iran should quickly agree to end the conflict or face broader attacks on energy infrastructure. At the same time, the White House said contacts with Tehran were still continuing, even as Iranian officials publicly denied any negotiations. The war has now widened into a broader regional crisis, damaging infrastructure and raising market concerns. Iran&#x27;s retaliation included a strike on an Israeli oil refinery and, according to NDTV&#x27;s live coverage, attacks that reached neighboring Gulf Arab states. Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Israel had achieved more than half of its military aims, but neither he nor President Trump gave a timeline for ending the campaign. What happens next remains unclear, but the coverage also points to active efforts to stop the fighting, including a reported regional meeting led by Pakistan and continued public discussion of talks. Even in a severe crisis, those channels suggest that diplomacy is still in play.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/FyUmlxvtazrvhFfc8z3m1ZSRvVoEU_a_FBZfjAzUDXkiHJzV6FtTzh-v3fSg2bZsyUR9XdKY_dPrBQVd9XbGCKbK9yrpbOpOlo_ywYyJRG7xcUzSdfAfAloz-qdWs6la5wqofi8HNkEQirZ5' alt='Image accompanying PBS reporting on Iran&#x27;s strike on an Israeli oil refinery during the widening regional war' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Death toll: NDTV reported that more than 3,000 people have been killed in the US-Israel-Iran war as retaliatory attacks spread beyond Iran and Israel.</li><li>Domestic crackdown: The Hindu&#x27;s live coverage said Iran executed two more people convicted of links to a banned opposition group as the conflict continued.</li><li>Hormuz pressure: The Hindu reported that President Trump was willing to end the war even if the Strait of Hormuz remained largely closed, underscoring the waterway&#x27;s central role in the crisis.</li></ul><blockquote>Much different than what’s being communicated to us privately - Karoline Leavitt</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>White House: Press secretary Karoline Leavitt said private messages from Tehran did not match its public denials and insisted that contacts were still continuing. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/636788-israel-war-tehran-strikes-us-live-updates/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Iranian officials: Iran&#x27;s ambassador to Russia, Kazem Jalali, rejected Trump&#x27;s claims of negotiations and mocked the idea, saying the US president was &quot;almost sitting in front of a mirror negotiating with himself.&quot; (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/636788-israel-war-tehran-strikes-us-live-updates/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Israeli government: Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Israel was already &#x27;beyond halfway point&#x27; in achieving its war aims, but still gave no timeline for ending the operation. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/31/netanyahu-iran-war-usa-trump'>Euronews</a>)</li><li>President Trump: President Trump said Tehran should quickly agree to end the war or risk wider attacks on Iranian power plants and oil hubs. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/iran-hits-israeli-oil-refinery-as-trump-escalates-threats-in-widening-regional-war'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/636788-israel-war-tehran-strikes-us-live-updates/'>Israel rocks Tehran with wave of strikes while Washington insists ‘talks continue’ (PHOTOS, VIDEOS)</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/iran-hits-israeli-oil-refinery-as-trump-escalates-threats-in-widening-regional-war'>Iran hits Israeli oil refinery as Trump escalates threats in widening regional war</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-israel-iran-war-updates-live-march-31-2026/article70805560.ece'>Iran-Israe